<title>UK: Unichem sells Lloyds stake.</title>
<headline>Unichem sells Lloyds stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British pharmaceutical group Unichem Plc sold its shares in chemists chain Lloyds Chemists Plc on Monday, brokers UBS Limited said.</p>
<p>In a disclosure statement, UBS said it sold 12,276,181 ordinary shares in Lloyds at 525p per share on Unichem's behalf. It said Unichem now held no shares in Lloyds.</p>
<p>Earlier on Monday German pharmaceutical group Gehe AG ended its year-long battle with Unichem for control of Lloyds. Gehe bought a majority in Lloyds at 525p per share, valuing the British group at 684 million pounds.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
